From 2d526339bc516dc1ebbcb1946d67b8ce23ab9d57 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: easymesh-clients <noreply@vcpe.dev>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 11:25:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Roaming by a fixed margin, a margin while active, and
 staying above a trigger

Network options roam_margin, roam_margin_active, roam_active_pps and
roam_trigger. With roam_margin set, the in-ESS decision moves only when the
candidate is heard at least that many dB stronger than the current BSS (the
active margin while the station transmitted roam_active_pps packets per second
since the previous decision; received packets include beacons, so are not
counted). With roam_trigger set, scan results do not move the station while
the current BSS is above it, unless a background scan module reported a load
trigger; a BSS Transition Management request is not affected. All default to
0, which keeps the built-in decision. CTRL-EVENT-DO-ROAM and
CTRL-EVENT-SKIP-ROAM say which rule acted.
---
 wpa_supplicant/config.c           |   4 ++
 wpa_supplicant/config_file.c      |   4 ++
 wpa_supplicant/config_ssid.h      |  36 +++++++++++
 wpa_supplicant/events.c           | 101 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 wpa_supplicant/wpa_supplicant_i.h |   9 +++
 5 files changed, 154 insertions(+)

